id: pm-starter-4n5o
title: "The changelog gate stamps an untagged version with the current date, so its verdict flips every midnight with no commit"
description: "Root cause of the test 22 and test 26 failures that blocked pull requests 71, 72 and 73. Two independent causes, both downstream of the npm publish outage. First, the release workflow pushes the release tag only after npm publish succeeds. Publish has been failing since 2026-08-21, so versions 2026.8.22 through 2026.8.24 have release commits on main and no tags. For a version with no tag, pm-changelog synthesises a pending release window and stamps it with the current UTC date rather than anything derived from the input, so changelog check regenerates a different heading date every day and fails on any day after the changelog was generated. Measured directly: with the version set to an untagged 2026.8.20 the generator emits heading 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-24, today's date. The fix is the existing --date-from-version flag, which derives the no-tag fallback from the calendar version itself; verified on pm-ops that an untagged 2026.8.22 then emits 2026-08-22 rather than today. No fleet package passed that flag. Second, the exact devDependency pin on the pm CLI at 2026.8.15 violates pm-changelog 2026.8.17's peer requirement of at least 2026.8.16, so npm ci fails with ERESOLVE before any test runs. Fixed by pinning 2026.8.23 and floating pm-changelog to at least 2026.8.17. Rejected an earlier fix that backfilled the three missing git tags: the release workflow deliberately tags only after a successful publish, so a backfilled tag asserts a release npm never received, and it would have hidden the clock dependence rather than removing it. Those tags were pushed and have been deleted."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: changelog,gates,release
created_at: "2026-08-24T09:04:29.067Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T09:18:27.067Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T09:04:48.740Z","harness:claude-code","Verification, both directions, on this repo with pm-changelog 2026.8.17 installed. Without the flag, an untagged version 2026.8.20 generates the heading 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-24, which is today rather than anything derived from the version. With the flag the version drives the sectioning instead. Cross-checked the same mechanism on pm-ops, where an untagged 2026.8.22 generates 2026-08-22 with the flag and 2026-08-24 without it, which is the decisive comparison because there the version date and today's date differ. Gates after the change: npm test 169 pass 0 fail, coverage 100.00 line 100.00 branch 100.00 funcs with the gate reporting thresholds met, pinned pm health --strict-exit exit 0, changelog:full followed by changelog:check reports up to date."
  "2026-08-24T09:18:27.067Z","harness:claude-code","Incomplete on the first pass, caught by Sourcery and Greptile independently on pull request 77, and both were right. I had patched only the package.json changelog scripts. The release workflow invokes pm-changelog directly at three more sites, and package.json carried a fourth in release:notes that I missed because I only looked at scripts whose name begins with changelog. That left generation and check disagreeing on exactly the input the flag governs: on an untagged version whose calendar date is not today, release.yml would generate a heading from the clock and CI would then check it with the version-derived flag, so the release would fail on the divergence the change was supposed to remove. Enumerated properly this time rather than pattern-matching on script names: grep for release-version-from-package across every tracked file finds seven sites in this package, four in package.json and three in release.yml, and all seven now carry the flag. Recount confirms four of four and three of three. Gates after the completion: npm test 169 pass 0 fail, changelog full then check reports up to date, release:notes exits 0 once GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY is set as it is in CI, pinned pm health --strict-exit exit 0. Recording the miss because the lesson generalises: the flag is a property of every invocation of the generator, and a fix applied to the surface an agent happened to read is not the same as a fix applied to the class."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,changelog scripts gain date-from-version; pm CLI devDependency pinned to 2026.8.23 and pm-changelog floated to at least 2026.8.17
  package-lock.json,project,lockfile resolution for the corrected pins
tests[3]{command,path,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
  "npm run changelog:check",package.json,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-08-24T09:05:38.285Z",local_mutation,fix/stabilise-changelog-date-and-unpin-cli-devdep,fails when the no-tag fallback date is stamped from the clock; passes once --date-from-version derives it from the calendar version
  npm test,.,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-08-24T09:05:38.285Z",local_mutation,fix/stabilise-changelog-date-and-unpin-cli-devdep,"169 pass 0 fail once the pm CLI pin satisfies the pm-changelog peer requirement, so npm ci no longer dies with ERESOLVE"
  npm run coverage,.,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-08-24T09:05:38.285Z",local_mutation,fix/stabilise-changelog-date-and-unpin-cli-devdep,"coverage-gate reports 3 source files at 100.00 line 100.00 branch 100.00 funcs, thresholds met"
body: ""
